<p><hr align=left size=1 noshade width="100%"><p>
<h1><a name="V-section">V</a></h1>


<p><b><a name="value_function">Value Function</a></b> &nbsp; &nbsp;
A built-in <a href="glossary-F.html#function">function</a> in <a href="glossary-L.html#lisp">Lisp</a> or <a href="glossary-S.html#stutter">Stutter</a> that evaluates
all of its arguments prior to being executed, e.g., <tt>car</tt>, 
<tt>cdr</tt>, and <tt>cons</tt>.  

<p><b><a name="vant">Vant</a></b> &nbsp; &nbsp;
A virtual ant; a type of <a href="glossary-C.html#cellular_automaton_(ca)">cellular automaton</a> that vaguely emulates
the activity of one or more ants.  

<p><b><a name="variation">Variation</a></b> &nbsp; &nbsp;
Genetic differences among individuals in a population.  

<p><b><a name="vector">Vector</a></b> &nbsp; &nbsp;
A one-dimensional array of numbers that can be used to represent a
point in a multidimensional space.  



